INT. HALVORSEN-BRAND INC. - OPEN-PLAN OFFICE, "SYNERGY POD" - DAY

Rows of beige desks. A foosball table nobody uses. A banner reads "WE ARE FAMILY (TERMS APPLY)."

MR. HALVORSEN, fifties, in a vest and a tie with tiny fish, stands at a whiteboard. BRENDA, forties, his office manager, stands beside him with a laser pointer. CHIP, thirties, loud, and DUTCH, forties, soft-spoken, share a desk. GWEN, twenties, scribbles in a notebook.

A NEW HIRE, twenties, a laptop bag on one shoulder, hovers by the door with a lanyard around her neck.

MR. HALVORSEN
Team! Team! Please welcome our latest synergist.

Scattered applause. Chip whoops.

CHIP
Welcome to the family!

BRENDA
(under her breath)
Terms apply.

MR. HALVORSEN
And you are?

NEW HIRE
Priya.

MR. HALVORSEN
Priya! A name like a poem. Where do you want to sit?

PRIYA
Wherever there's an outlet.

CHIP
The outlets are communal, Priya.

DUTCH
We're sharing three between thirty.

PRIYA
How do you charge anything?

DUTCH
We rotate. It builds trust.

GWEN
(without looking up)
It builds bruises. Steve's still limping from Tuesday.

MR. HALVORSEN
Gwen, we agreed on positivity.

GWEN
I'm positive he's limping.

BRENDA
Mr. Halvorsen, the onboarding packet?

MR. HALVORSEN
Right. Priya, you'll receive a binder, a mug, and a mission statement.

PRIYA
I'd rather have a desk.

MR. HALVORSEN
The desk is earned.

PRIYA
How?

CHIP
Three quarters of exceeding metrics.

PRIYA
What are the metrics?

DUTCH
Nobody knows.

BRENDA
(sharp)
Dutch.

DUTCH
Sorry. They're confidential.

PRIYA
To whom?

MR. HALVORSEN
To me, mostly.

Priya looks around. The team looks at the floor. The foosball table creaks as no one touches it.

PRIYA
So I show up for two years, to a job I can't define, for a desk I can't have.

MR. HALVORSEN
It's a journey.

CHIP
A beautiful journey.

BRENDA
She doesn't have to say yes, Chip.

GWEN
(still writing)
She does. They all do.

Priya laughs, short, appalled. She slides the laptop bag off her shoulder and sets it on the foosball table.

PRIYA
Fine. I'll stand.

MR. HALVORSEN
Wonderful!

DUTCH
You can use my outlet, Priya. Mondays.

PRIYA
Thank you, Dutch.

CHIP
Look at that! Already a family.

BRENDA
Terms apply, Chip.

Mr. Halvorsen beams at the whiteboard, where somebody has drawn a lopsided tree.

MR. HALVORSEN
Now, who wants to hear about our Q3 vision?

Nobody does. Everyone nods anyway.
